# Normalize text to LF in the repo -- both stored blobs and worktree
# checkouts. This is what M2b's line-ending fix (docs/07-ROADMAP.md)
# applies -- the pre-existing schema-freshness/resolve-preview-url CRLF
# bug class came from core.autocrlf=true with no .gitattributes at all,
# which let a Windows checkout silently diverge from the committed (LF)
# blobs. Fixtures are included, not exempted: leaving them to
# core.autocrlf would let this exact class of corruption reach captured
# response bytes on the next `git add`. eol=lf (not text=auto's platform
# default) keeps checkouts LF on every OS, matching what Linux CI already
# sees, so a contentHash computed locally never disagrees with CI's.
* text=auto eol=lf
